```markdown
# Awakened PoE Trade

[![License](https://img.shields.io/github/license/SnosMe/awakened-poe-trade)](./LICENSE)
[![GitHub Releases](https://img.shields.io/github/downloads/SnosMe/awakened-poe-trade/total)](https://github.com/SnosMe/awakened-poe-trade/releases)

**Awakened PoE Trade** is a fast, modular, and open-source overlay tool for Path of Exile. It provides essential trading and utility features designed to enhance the player experience without breaking immersion.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 💰 **Instant Price Check** – Evaluate item values using live market data directly in-game.
- 🗺️ **Map Check** – Quickly identify dangerous modifiers on maps and highlight your preferred mods.
- 🔍 **Stash Search** – Search through your stash tabs with ease using advanced filters.
- 💎 **Vision-Based Tools** – Includes a specialized Heist Gem Finder using OCR technology.
- 🌐 **Multi-Language Support** – Full support for English, Traditional Chinese (繁體中文), Korean (한국어), and Russian (Русский).
- 🛠️ **Customizable Overlay** – A modern UI built with Vue 3 that adapts to your workflow.

## 🚀 Getting Started

### For Users
1. Download the latest version from the [Releases Page](https://github.com/SnosMe/awakened-poe-trade/releases).
2. Run the application; it will automatically detect your Path of Exile client.
3. Use the default hotkeys (e.g., `Ctrl + D` for price check) to interact with the overlay.

### For Developers
The project is split into a **Main** (Electron) and **Renderer** (Vue 3) architecture.

1. **Prerequisites**: Node.js and Yarn/NPM.
2. **Setup**:
   - Navigate to `/main` and run `npm install`.
   - Navigate to `/renderer` and run `npm install`.
3. **Execution**: Refer to [DEVELOPING.md](./DEVELOPING.md) for detailed run/build commands.

## 🛠️ Technical Stack

- **Core**: [Electron](https://www.electronjs.org/)
- **Frontend**: [Vue 3](https://vuejs.org/) + [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/)
- **Styling**: [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)
- **Language**: TypeScript

## 📚 Documentation

Detailed guides are available in the `/docs` folder:
- [Quick Start Guide](./docs/quick-start.md)
- [Chat Commands](./docs/chat-commands.md)
- [FAQ & Troubleshooting](./docs/faq.md)
- [Taiwan Server Setup](./TWServer.md)

## 🤝 Contributing

Contributions are welcome! Please read our [Development Guide](./DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md) before submitting pull requests.

---

*Disclaimer: This tool is not affiliated with or endorsed by Grinding Gear Games.*
```

